    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d62">

                <pb facs="0165" n="69" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg69"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Señor Infante.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-06-05"><hi rendition="#italic">June 5,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 16.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Vicuna’s note of January
                    27 last, I have the honor to state that the attorney for the heirs of Patrick
                    Shields is pressing the Department to ascertain when payment will be made of
                    their claim.</p>
                <p>I have, therefore, the honor to ask that the arrangement reached may be promptly
                    carried out by your Government.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
